# Engineering Architecture

## Stack

Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict mode, Tailwind CSS, accessible component primitives, Lucide icons, Zustand or lightweight reducer state, localStorage persistence, a local deterministic adaptation engine, static media assets, and a local illustrated map or SVG.

Do not require external API keys, a production database, auth provider, payment processor, map provider, or live AI service for v0.1.

## Structure

Prefer:

```text
src/
├── app/
├── components/
│   ├── shared/
│   ├── creator/
│   ├── learner/
│   ├── orchestrator/
│   └── review/
├── data/
├── lib/
├── hooks/
├── store/
├── types/
└── assets/
```

## State

Persist selected role, selected learner, learner progress, Field Notes, confidence, adaptive branch, mentor interventions, systems map, artifact, and resurfacing completion.

Provide a reliable demo reset.

## Simulated intelligence

Keep adaptation rules pure and testable. Inputs should include learner profile, current stop, recent Field Notes, confidence, evidence count, inactivity simulation, mentor override, and accessibility preferences.

Outputs should include recommended prompt, reason, category, severity, and optional creator-authored fallback.

## Code quality

- avoid `any`
- centralize canonical mock data
- keep components focused
- do not duplicate journey text
- use meaningful names
- handle loading, empty, and error states
- do not over-engineer backend abstractions

## Validation

Every milestone must run:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run build
```
